  "question": {
    "text": "Let $a_0, a_1, \\ldots, a_{23}$ be real numbers such that\n$\\left(1+\\frac{2}{5} x\\right)^{23}=\\sum_{i=0}^{23} a_i x^i$\nfor every real number $x$. let $a_r$ be the largest among the numbers $a_j$ for $0 \\leq j \\leq 23$.\nThe the value of $r$ is ______",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "6",
  "solution": {
    "text": "For $\\mathrm{x}=1$\n$\\left(1+\\frac{2}{5}\\right)^{23}=a_0+a_1+a_2+\\ldots+a_{23}$\nfor numerically greatest term\n$\\frac{n+1}{1+\\left|\\frac{a}{b}\\right|}=\\frac{23+1}{1+\\frac{5}{2}}=\\frac{48}{7}$\n$\\Rightarrow\\left[\\frac{48}{7}\\right]=6=\\mathrm{m}$ (where [.] greatest integer function)\nso, $\\mathrm{T}_7$ is numerical greatest term\nHence $r=6$",
    "image": null
  },
